      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have confirmed this solution and found this question too.The problem is because I  have removed AAudioStreamBuilder_setErrorCallback in BtifAvrcpAudioErrorHandle last time, it seems like AAudio just call ErrorCallback only once, we must setErrorCallback again if we want to it works.\n\nSo AAudioStreamBuilder_setErrorCallback must be set in the BtifAvrcpAudioErrorHandle, in order to AAudio will call ErrorCallback when error occur next time\n\n\n\nAnd the concern you mentioned last time, I have checked in my environment, the thread will be created only when the last BtifAvrcpAudioErrorHandle finished(if (s_AudioEngine.thread \u003d\u003d nullptr)), it will ensure the new thread won\u0027t be recreated",
